  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>8</mn><mtext>th&#160;</mtext></msup></math> common term of the series<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>. is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "151",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>Two A.P&#39;s&nbsp; as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;</p><p>First term<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Common difference<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>And,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math>,</p><p>First term<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Common difference&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Now, common difference of the series of the common terms of the given A.P&#39;s is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>LCM</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>LCM</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p>Now, series of common term is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>51</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>71</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>8</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;common&nbsp;term appearing in the both the series is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>151</mn></math></p>",
